    {
      "id": "claim_e6af3dfdf1134aeca75c8c9d6e475e75",
      "statement": "WarehouseFactory.get_warehouse_client(org_warehouse) is the primary entrypoint: it raises ValueError if the warehouse is falsy or its credentials cannot be retrieved, fetches credentials via retrieve_warehouse_credentials, and delegates to connect(creds, wtype), which builds PostgresClient for postgres, BigqueryClient for bigquery, and raises ValueError otherwise.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/ddpui/utils/warehouse/client/warehouse_factory.py#L9-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8f02a7afa59591c626c8d8961f300af160cf19682464c89110e43b27fc12a767:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/ddpui/utils/warehouse/client/warehouse_interface.py#L5-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:65570745cc4ba9300f056a529594aad81be53728af0d5dcb7f141cd8200e8487:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_df072a49e51745a9ba5a65acedee7278",
      "statement": "The Warehouse ABC defines only execute, get_table_columns, get_col_python_type, get_wtype and column_exists; execute returns list[dict] rows keyed by column alias and takes raw SQL without exposed parameter binding, while callers compile AggQueryBuilder statements against the client's .engine with literal binds.",
